egin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -2 & -12\\end{aligned}|=-6$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -2 & -12\\end{aligned}|=-54$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -2 & -12\\end{aligned}|=18$" 13194139535210 true] [17592186120366 1145 "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =20-2 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -2 & -12\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ -3 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -2 & -12\\end{aligned}|}{18} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -2 & -12\\end{aligned}| & =-54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"." 13194139535210 true] [17592186120373 1017 #edb/ref 17592186118713 13194139535210 false] [17592186120373 1017 #edb/ref 17592186337725 13194139535210 true] [17592186120373 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535210 true] [17592186120373 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n${7x - 2y = 10; - 2x + y = 8$.\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $x$ can be written as\n$x = \\frac{D_{x}}{\\begin{vmatrix}7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}}$, where $D_{x} =$" 13194139535210 false] [17592186120373 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\,7x-2y=10 \\\\ -2x+y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $x$ can be written as \n$x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{|\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|}$, where ${D}_{x}=$" 13194139535210 true] [17592186120373 1145 "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}7x-2y=10 \\\\ -2x+y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by t